se Zinc's stronger analysis:\n\u002F\u002F   incOptions ~= (_.withRecompileAllFraction(1.0))\n",[20,1272,1273,1278,1283,1287,1292,1297,1302,1307,1312,1316,1321,1326,1331],{"__ignoreMap":30},[34,1274,1275],{"class":36,"line":37},[34,1276,1277],{"class":40},"\u002F\u002F Symptom: sbt says \"compiling 0 files\" but you changed a trait method\n",[34,1279,1280],{"class":36,"line":44},[34,1281,1282],{"class":40},"\u002F\u002F signature that downstream modules use. Tests fail with NoSuchMethodError.\n",[34,1284,1285],{"class":36,"line":50},[34,1286,140],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":139},[34,1288,1289],{"class":36,"line":56},[34,1290,1291],{"class":40},"\u002F\u002F Root cause: sbt's incremental compiler tracks API signatures, but\n",[34,1293,1294],{"class":36,"line":62},[34,1295,1296],{"class":40},"\u002F\u002F renaming a method while keeping the same erased signature (e.g.\n",[34,1298,1299],{"class":36,"line":68},[34,1300,1301],{"class":40},"\u002F\u002F def process(items: List[Int]) → def process(items: Seq[Int]))\n",[34,1303,1304],{"class":36,"line":77},[34,1305,1306],{"class":40},"\u002F\u002F can miss the downstream recompile because the erased signature is\n",[34,1308,1309],{"class":36,"line":86},[34,1310,1311],{"class":40},"\u002F\u002F identical (List → Seq both erase to scala.collection.immutable.Seq).\n",[34,1313,1314],{"class":36,"line":305},[34,1315,140],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":139},[34,1317,1318],{"class":36,"line":311},[34,1319,1320],{"class":40},"\u002F\u002F Fix: force clean for erased-signature changes\n",[34,1322,1323],{"class":36,"line":317},[34,1324,1325],{"class":40},"\u002F\u002F   sbt clean compile\n",[34,1327,1328],{"class":36,"line":549},[34,1329,1330],{"class":40},"\u002F\u002F Or use Zinc's stronger analysis:\n",[34,1332,1333],{"class":36,"line":554},[34,1334,1335],{"class":40},"\u002F\u002F   incOptions ~= (_.withRecompileAllFraction(1.0))\n",[1337,1338,1339,1343,1356],"details",{},[1340,1341,1342],"summary",{},"Answer",[1344,1345,1346,1347,1350,1351,1355],"p",{},"The ",[20,1348,1349],{},"NoSuchMethodError"," at runtime happens because Zinc (sbt's incremental compiler) uses ",[1352,1353,1354],"strong",{},"name + erased signature"," for staleness detection. When two different source-level signatures erase to the same bytecode signature, Zinc doesn't detect the change in downstream modules.",[1344,1357,1358,1361,1362,1365,1366,1369,1370,213],{},[1352,1359,1360],{},"Fix",": Run ",[20,1363,1364],{},"sbt clean compile"," for signature-level refactors, or configure ",[20,1367,1368],{},"incOptions"," with stricter recompile triggers in ",[20,1371,1372],{},"build.sbt",[15,1374,1376],{"id":1375},"tips-tricks","💡 Tips & Tricks",[1344,1378,1379,1385],{},[1352,1380,1381,1384],{},[20,1382,1383],{},"-Xprint:typer"," for debugging type inference failures",": The compiler dumps the fully-typed AST — you see exactly what types it inferred at each step, exposing where inference diverges from your expectation.",[94,1387,1388],{"language":96},[25,1389,1391],{"className":99,"code":1390,"language":96,"meta":30,"style":30},"# Show typed AST to debug \"found vs required\" errors\nscala-cli compile . --scalac-option \"-Xprint:typer\" 2>&1 | grep -A5 \"myMethod\"\n",[20,1392,1393,1398],{"__ignoreMap":30},[34,1394,1395],{"class":36,"line":37},[34,1396,1397],{"class":40},"# Show typed AST to debug \"found vs required\" errors\n",[34,1399,1400,1402,1404,1406,1409,1412,1414,1416,1419,1422],{"class":36,"line":44},[34,1401,332],{"class":112},[34,1403,732],{"class":120},[34,1405,337],{"class":120},[34,1407,1408],{"class":116}," --scalac-option",[34,1410,1411],{"class":120}," \"-Xprint:typer\"",[34,1413,125],{"class":124},[34,1415,128],{"class":124},[34,1417,1418],{"class":112}," grep",[34,1420,1421],{"class":116}," -A5",[34,1423,1424],{"class":120}," \"myMethod\"\n",[1344,1426,1427,1430,1431,1434],{},[1352,1428,1429],{},"Coursier for reproducible toolchain",": Use ",[20,1432,1433],{},"cs"," (Coursier) to bootstrap Scala, sbt, and scalafmt — avoids Homebrew version drift across CI machines.",[94,1436,1437],{"language":96},[25,1438,1440],{"className":99,"code":1439,"language":96,"meta":30,"style":30},"# Pin everything via Coursier — CI uses identical versions\ncs install scala3 sbt scalafmt\ncs launch scalafmt:3.8.3 -- --test src\u002F   # format check in CI\n",[20,1441,1442,1447,1463],{"__ignoreMap":30},[34,1443,1444],{"class":36,"line":37},[34,1445,1446],{"class":40},"# Pin everything via Coursier — CI uses identical versions\n",[34,1448,1449,1451,1454,1457,1460],{"class":36,"line":44},[34,1450,1433],{"class":112},[34,1452,1453],{"class":120}," install",[34,1455,1456],{"class":120}," scala3",[34,1458,1459],{"class":120}," sbt",[34,1461,1462],{"class":120}," scalafmt\n",[34,1464,1465,1467,1470,1473,1475,1478,1481],{"class":36,"line":50},[34,1466,1433],{"class":112},[34,1468,1469],{"class":120}," launch",[34,1471,1472],{"class":120}," scalafmt:3.8.3",[34,1474,351],{"class":116},[34,1476,1477],{"class":116}," --test",[34,1479,1480],{"class":120}," src\u002F",[34,1482,1483],{"class":40},"   # format check in CI\n",[1344,1485,1486,1492],{},[1352,1487,1488,1491],{},[20,1489,1490],{},"-explain"," in Scala 3 gives human-readable type errors",": Far more actionable than the terse Scala 2 messages.",[15,1494,1496],{"id":1495},"️-edge-cases-gotchas","⚠️ Edge Cases & Gotchas",[1344,1498,1499,1502,1503,1506,1507,1509],{},[1352,1500,1501],{},"Scala 2 and Scala 3 cannot share the same binary artifact",": Scala 2.13 and 3.x have different TASTy\u002Fclassfile formats. For cross-published libraries, use ",[20,1504,1505],{},"%%"," (cross-built) not ",[20,1508,1505],{}," with a hardcoded version.",[1344,1511,1512,1517,1518,1521,1522,1524,1525,1528],{},[1352,1513,1514,1516],{},[20,1515,800],{}," initialization is lazy",": The ",[20,1519,1520],{},"MODULE$"," singleton initializes on first access, not at class-load time. Side effects in ",[20,1523,800],{}," bodies run at an unpredictable time — use ",[20,1526,1527],{},"@main"," or explicit initialization.",[1344,1530,1531,1537,1538,1541],{},[1352,1532,1533,1536],{},[20,1534,1535],{},"-Werror"," + Scala 2 macro libraries",": Macro expansions can produce warnings that become errors. Use ",[20,1539,1540],{},"-Wconf:cat=unused:silent"," to suppress warnings from generated code.",[1344,1543,1544,1547,1548,1551,1552,1555,1556,1558,1559,1562,1563,1566,1567,1570],{},[1352,1545,1546],{},"JVM target mismatch",": If ",[20,1549,1550],{},"scalaVersion"," targets JVM 17 but your ",[20,1553,1554],{},"JAVA_HOME"," is JDK 11, ",[20,1557,729],{}," fails with ",[20,1560,1561],{},"UnsupportedClassVersionError",". Pin ",[20,1564,1565],{},"javaOptions"," and ",[20,1568,1569],{},"fork := true"," to control the JVM version sbt uses for running.",[15,1572,1574],{"id":1573},"quick-quiz","🧠 Quick Quiz",[1344,1576,1577,1578,1581],{},"What does ",[20,1579,1580],{},"scalac -Xprint:delambdafy"," show, and why does it matter for performance?",[1337,1583,1584,1586,1596,1619],{},[1340,1585,1342],{},[1344,1587,1588,1591,1592,1595],{},[20,1589,1590],{},"-Xprint:delambdafy"," shows how the compiler desugars lambdas (",[20,1593,1594],{},"x => x * 2",") into JVM constructs:",[1597,1598,1599,1610],"ul",{},[1600,1601,1602,1605,1606,1609],"li",{},[1352,1603,1604],{},"Non-capturing lambdas"," → a singleton ",[20,1607,1608],{},"$$Lambda$"," object (zero allocation per call).",[1600,1611,1612,1615,1616,1618],{},[1352,1613,1614],{},"Capturing lambdas"," → a new ",[20,1617,1608],{}," instance per invocation, capturing free variables as fields.",[1344,1620,1621,1622,1625,1626,1628],{},"This matters for hot paths: a lambda capturing ",[20,1623,1624],{},"this"," allocates on every call. In performance-critical code, hoist the lambda to a ",[20,1627,921],{}," or use a non-capturing method reference.",[1630,1631,1632],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .sdCPZ, html code.shiki .sdCPZ{--shiki-default:#6A737D;--shiki-github-dark:#6A737D}html .default .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);ba